# Build artifacts that `git add -A` will otherwise sweep into a commit. This has
# happened twice on this branch, once pulling in an agent's in-progress files and
# once a directory of build output. Stage by explicit path; these are the backstop.
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Eval transcripts are evidence and they are large: one run of the full matrix is
# 36 models x 15 questions. What is committed is the SUMMARY of every run -- the
# routing scorecards, the per-run manifests and RUNS.md -- plus the full
# transcripts of the run marked `final` in RUNS.md. Exploratory runs stay local;
# RUNS.md still records that they happened, and why they were superseded.
# See evals/README.md, "What is committed and what is not".
evals/runs/**/q*.jsonl
!evals/runs/final/**

# Scratch patch scripts. How a change was made, not what the change is -- the
# commit message is the durable record. Committed once by accident on 17 Sep,
# in the very commit whose README says they are never committed.
evals/_patch*.py
_patch*.py
